{"summary":"Checkout‑API latency spiked after the 10:15 deployment of v4.17, reaching p95 ≈ 2150 ms and causing timeouts. The spike was caused by a drastic reduction in the database connection pool size and timeout.

root_cause":"The upgrade to orders-client v3 changed the orders‑db pool configuration from 50 connections with a 5 s acquire timeout to only 10 connections and a 2 s timeout, exhausting the pool during checkout.",
","root_cause":"The upgrade to orders-client v3 changed the orders‑db pool configuration from 50 connections with a 5 s acquire timeout to only 10 connections and a 2 s timeout, exhausting the pool during checkout.","suspect_service":"checkout-api","suspect_version":"v4.17","suspect_deployment_id":"DEP-88213","previous_version":"v4.16","evidence":[{"tool":"source_control__get_diff","finding":"Commit a91f3c2 changed orders-db pool to max_connections:10 and acquire_timeout_ms:2000."},{"tool":"database__get_connection_pool_stats","finding":"At 10:40, in_use=10, waiting=143, acquire_wait_p95_ms=1800, exceeding the new limit."},{"tool":"observability__query_latency","finding":"p95 latency jumped from 200 ms to 2150 ms within minutes of deployment."},{"tool":"observability__search_logs","finding":"212 ConnectionPoolTimeoutError logs in last 15 min indicate pool exhaustion."},{"tool":"observability__get_slow_trace","finding":"db.pool.acquire span lasted 1829 ms, dominating the 2142 ms checkout trace."}],"ruled_out":["Other services (payment-gateway, inventory-api) had no latency spikes; their deployments were earlier and stable.","The issue was not a network outage or external API failure; logs show only internal DB pool errors."],"confidence":"high"}
